A||||4||WampusCat||My new printer ROCKS!||||7||
Z||000000||WampusCat||06-05-2001||08:44 AM||||My 5 year old Cannon inkjet bit the dust last week so I went down to Best Buy to get another.  I picked up an Epson Photo Stylus 780 for $150, not expecting too much from a relatively inexpensive printer.  After printing out some 8X10's of images taken with a 2.1 megapixel digital camera on Photo quality paper, I'm amazed!  The quality is as good as a photo lab using 35mm negs and a projector-enlarger.  Maybe everybody else is aware of how good ink jets are nowadays but I guess I haven't looked at them for a few years.  If you do digital photography, this thing is phenomenal for the price.  Maybe now I should upgrade my computer from my 200mhz Pentium I and 32 meg of RAM.  <P>Steve, being dragged kicking and screaming into the 21's century.||||reg||7
Z||000001||FieroJoe||06-05-2001||09:48 AM||||We have a HP Photoprinter, a newer one, I think it is a 830 ci or something like that.  It prints pretty good photo quality pictures, taken with our digicam.  Its nowhere near what you can get from a 35mm film print, but I dont regularly print out pictures taken with my digicam, usually they're pics of something that I'm going to post.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sootah||06-05-2001||10:16 AM||||Anytime I want something printed out REAL nice I e-mail the image to my dad @ work and have him print it out on the color laser out there. WOW. Then, if I need it laminated I just have him run through the laminator they have out there. Does 10X the job you could do by hand.<P>------------------<BR>Never argue with an idiot, they drag you down to their level and then beat you with experience||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||06-06-2001||12:51 AM||||WampusCat, Ive used Epson printers a lot. They are good printers, but Do Not like sitting idle.Not many ink jets do, but the ink in an Epson seems to dry up in the printhead easier & faster than most. Make sure you use it at least once every 2-3 wks.<BR>Printer prices have gone way down, but the ink cartridges haven't.$45 for color on my xerox & 32 for my Epson. What kind of memory you lookin for? I have two sticks of 16 meg<BR>I think it's pc100, I'd hafta look.Email me if you are interested.<BR>Don<p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 06-06-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000004||FieroSTETZ||06-08-2001||03:14 AM||||epson makes some nice printers, unfortunately, there was no thinking going on when they decided to make the printhead an integral part of the printer, as opposed to making it a part of the cartridge. believe it or not, the best bang for the buck printer i have seen is the lexmark z52 - niiiiice printer (i have a store with more than 40 printers to play with) I personally have a thermal bonding printer for photos, but lets not talk about the cost of that...<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.shawnrocks.com/Animation1.gif"> ||||reg||1
